## Choices
C01. Records root: a new `tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="pb-rehearsal-0510-")` in the system temp directory, outside every Git tree. Its absolute path is recorded. The tool writes only there. The request, registry and answers are written as plain input files in a sibling `inputs/` folder in that root.
C02. Registry `prime-support-registry` v1, in the accepted fixture form:
- one repository `workshop`: local D:/Git/lib-build, branch workshop, remote_ref refs/remotes/origin/workshop, worktree registered-paths, history_limit 50;
- one lane `0507.prime-support`, page folder `00.kernel/00.00.10.work/0507.prime-support`, with no return files and no review sources;
- canonical_assignment `{repository workshop, path …/0401.goal/06.01.md, lane 0507.prime-support}`.
No Clerk jobs. It is a pilot input, not an installation.
C03. Request `prime-boot-request/1`:
- role `Prime` as an exercise label; model `claude-opus-5-5`;
- book `00.kernel/00.00.10.work`;
- role_record `0408.seats/01.md`, assignment_record `0401.goal/06.01.md`;
- members `["0126.boot-members-0509"]`, with members_book the absolute work book;
- the packet lists the five full relative paths in batch order;
- limits 12 refs and 131072 bytes;
- the tools are the absolute paths of the pinned files in this workspace.
C04. Answers: O1-O6, written by me only from the recorded packet, with citations. Each answer separates what the packet shows from what I already know from this session. A stale canonical record or a conflict is stated, not hidden.
C05. `check` only. No `judge`, and no 30, 31 or 39 file. A retry is used only for a documented transient identity change or a request-construction mistake, and links the first attempt.
C06. records.json: version `prime-boot-rehearsal-records/1`. It is a file map of every file under the records root, the inputs, and the raw stdout and stderr of every command. Each entry gives a logical name, a base64 encoding of the bytes, the byte count and the sha256.
C07. Read-only proof: before and after the runs, I snapshot the sha256 of every packet source in the worktree, the whole 0126 member folder, `git rev-parse HEAD`, refs/heads/workshop and the `git status --porcelain` lines. Changes from other lanes are told apart by path: the only writes authorised for this batch are 05.10.md, 06.11.md and evidence/rehearsal05.10/.

